        "original_id": "0ea12b57-0ec4-515a-9206-3eab0d9e221b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeremy Brock, Kevin Macdonald, Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, Donald Sutherland, Rosemary Sutcliff\n- Works: The Eagle, The Eagle of the Ninth, Mrs Brown, Driving Lessons, The Last King of Scotland, Charlotte Gray\n- Topics: film adaptation, Roman Britain\n\nFacts:\n- Jeremy Brock was born in 1959 and is an English writer and director.\n- Jeremy Brock's works include the screenplays for Mrs Brown, Driving Lessons, The Last King of Scotland, Charlotte Gray, and The Eagle.\n- Rosemary Sutcliff published the historical adventure novel The Eagle of the Ninth in 1954.\n- The Eagle is a 2011 epic historical drama film set in Roman Britain.\n- Kevin Macdonald directed The Eagle.\n- Channing Tatum, Jamie Bell, and Donald Sutherland starred in The Eagle.\n- Jeremy Brock adapted The Eagle from Rosemary Sutcliff's novel The Eagle of the Ninth.\n- The Eagle tells the story of a young Roman officer searching northern Great Britain for the lost Roman eagle standard of his father's legion.",
